# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Leave this UNSET to use Netlify Forms. That is the default and needs no
# configuration at all — Netlify provisions the handler when it deploys the
# site. It only works on Netlify.
#
# SET it to switch the form over to Formspree, which works on any host
# (Vercel, Cloudflare Pages, GitHub Pages, plain static hosting). Sign up at
# formspree.io, create a form, and paste its endpoint here — the whole URL,
# not just the ID:
#
# PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
#
# The PUBLIC_ prefix is Astro's, and it means this value is compiled into the
# client bundle. That is correct for a Formspree form ID, which is public by
# design. Never put a secret behind that prefix.

# PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=
